s.com/story/diesel-prices-down-in-nova-scotia-p-e-i-fe8c0dd2ce/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/diesel-prices-down-in-nova-scotia-p-e-i-fe8c0dd2ce/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:20:48 +0000</pubDate><category>Fuel</category><description>Diesel prices fell overnight in Nova Scotia, and both diesel and gasoline changed on Prince Edward Island. In the Halifax area, the minimum diesel price dropped 7.5 cents to 225.9 cents per litre, while diesel in Cape Breton stood at 227.8 cents per litre. On P.E.I., regular gasoline fell four cents to 155.7 cents per litre and the minimum diesel price decreased 5.7 cents to 227.4. New Brunswick prices held, with maximum gasoline at 161.6 cents and maximum diesel at 241.4 cents per litre. The next scheduled adjustment across the three Maritime provinces is Friday. Chris McKee, executive director of the Atlantic Provinces Trucking Association, said diesel has seen &quot;fairly significant reductions&quot; since September but remains elevated. Petroleum analyst Patrick De Haan said prices could keep falling depending on geopolitical issues, and he hoped they would drop below $2 a litre at some point.</description></item><item><title>Good faith in trucking insurance claims</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/good-faith-in-trucking-insurance-claims-6783264813/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/good-faith-in-trucking-insurance-claims-6783264813/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:00:51 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Trucker-built directory tops 12,000 listings as roadside repair network expands</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-built-directory-tops-12-000-listings-as-roadside-repair-networ-335f0fc202/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-built-directory-tops-12-000-listings-as-roadside-repair-networ-335f0fc202/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>60pc of Northern Corridor truck drivers sick: Report</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/60pc-of-northern-corridor-truck-drivers-sick-report-89f2ac98fb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/60pc-of-northern-corridor-truck-drivers-sick-report-89f2ac98fb/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>The EastAfrican</description></item><item><title>Attention truckers: Brace for Thanksgiving traffic as nearly 73 million travelers hit the road</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/attention-truckers-brace-for-thanksgiving-traffic-as-nearly-73-million-afae035d53/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/attention-truckers-brace-for-thanksgiving-traffic-as-nearly-73-million-afae035d53/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:46:35 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>AAA projects that nearly 73 million Americans will travel by car between Nov. 24-30, and the National Safety Council estimates 428 people could die in motor vehicle crashes during the Thanksgiving holiday period. That fatality estimate is 2% lower than last year&#x27;s, but the council also projects 48,800 people could suffer injuries needing medical attention. INRIX expects the two days before Thanksgiving, Tuesday and Wednesday, plus Sunday and Monday afterward, to be busiest, with Thanksgiving Day itself lighter. The article advises truck drivers to add time to trip plans, expect sudden lane changes and sudden braking, leave extra following distance, and plan parking, fuel and meal stops around possible holiday closures. The council also estimates 104 more lives could be saved if all vehicle occupants wore seat belts.</description></item><item><title>Port of Oakland charging up 300 Tesla Semi trucks for zero-emission freight corridor</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/port-of-oakland-charging-up-300-tesla-semi-trucks-for-zero-emission-fr-0acecd0bcd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/port-of-oakland-charging-up-300-tesla-semi-trucks-for-zero-emission-fr-0acecd0bcd/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:05:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>&#x27;Keep that car until you are on the first-name basis with the tow truck drivers.&#x27;</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/keep-that-car-until-you-are-on-the-first-name-basis-with-the-tow-truck-f6f89a3054/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/keep-that-car-until-you-are-on-the-first-name-basis-with-the-tow-truck-f6f89a3054/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:38:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>The Washington Post</description></item><item><title>How Physical AI Can Help Control What Truckers Burn</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/how-physical-ai-can-help-control-what-truckers-burn-c80bf8c1dc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/how-physical-ai-can-help-control-what-truckers-burn-c80bf8c1dc/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:05:36 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>SupplyChainBrain</description></item><item><title>Truck Drivers Stage Protests Over Alleged Harassment</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truck-drivers-stage-protests-over-alleged-harassment-c8f15cfef9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truck-drivers-stage-protests-over-alleged-harassment-c8f15cfef9/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:57:38 +0000</pubDate><category>Drivers &amp; Jobs</category><description>Kenyans.co.ke</description></item><item><title>Motor carriers hurt by diesel costs</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/motor-carriers-hurt-by-diesel-costs-d2796de249/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/motor-carriers-hurt-by-diesel-costs-d2796de249/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:05:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Northwest Arkansas Democrat-Gazette</description></item><item><title>Connected Fleet Tech: Cutting Truck Downtime &amp; Maintenance Costs</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/connected-fleet-tech-cutting-truck-downtime-maintenance-costs-f52b94b9f7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/connected-fleet-tech-cutting-truck-downtime-maintenance-costs-f52b94b9f7/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:49:59 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Commercial Driver&#x27;s License: Nick Castello; Application for Exemption</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/commercial-driver-s-license-nick-castello-application-for-exemption-a0443343ed/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/commercial-driver-s-license-nick-castello-application-for-exemption-a0443343ed/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>The Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration is asking for public comment on an exemption application filed by Nick Castello. The request would let state licensing agencies issue non-domiciled commercial learner&#x27;s permits and CDLs to drivers in humanitarian or protection-based categories, including Uniting for Ukraine, Temporary Protected Status, asylum and pending asylum. The notice does not signal how the agency will decide; FMCSA will grant or deny the request after reviewing the application, safety analyses and comments.

The notice points to a final rule published February 13, 2026, which bars these permits and licenses unless the applicant shows lawful immigration status. The listed categories under that rule are H-2A, H-2B and E-2. Castello, described as a U.S. Marine Corps veteran and disabled veteran business owner, asks for relief of up to five years or a shorter period, and says he collected 93 responses from drivers reporting recurring problems with non-domiciled transactions. Comments are due December 24, 2026, under docket FMCSA-2026-3268.</description></item><item><title>Trucker Path app launches free CB radio feature</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-path-app-launches-free-cb-radio-feature-a2b6ef683e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-path-app-launches-free-cb-radio-feature-a2b6ef683e/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:26:27 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Diesel prices soar as Silicon Valley startup unveils cab-less trucking solution</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/diesel-prices-soar-as-silicon-valley-startup-unveils-cab-less-trucking-5c25dc2917/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/diesel-prices-soar-as-silicon-valley-startup-unveils-cab-less-trucking-5c25dc2917/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:27:06 +0000</pubDate><category>Fuel</category><description>Fox Business</description></item><item><title>CRST Drivers Win $1.8M In Truck Lease Case</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/crst-drivers-win-1-8m-in-truck-lease-case-dcc5f006b3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/crst-drivers-win-1-8m-in-truck-lease-case-dcc5f006b3/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:26:14 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>An Iowa federal judge awarded nearly $1.8 million to close to 1,000 drivers that CRST underpaid under their leases, rejecting the company&#x27;s bid to deny recovery o